        "Content": "\nWhite Gables House presents a rare opportunity to acquire an attractive detached residence of approximately 350 sq. m., set amid approximately 1 acre of secluded, mature grounds within a private gated community. Built in 1953, the house originally stood within a larger holding, portions of which were subsequently developed with high-quality detached homes to create the surrounding White Gables development. Importantly, the private developer ensured that the original residence retained extensive gardens, preserving its exceptional privacy and sense of seclusion. Electric entrance gates, located on a private road, open onto a sweeping tarmac driveway leading to a generous parking area and the house itself, which is well maintained and offers impressive proportions throughout.\n\nAn Outstanding Family Home: The accommodation includes spacious reception rooms, a well-appointed kitchen, utility room, home office, five bedrooms and three bathrooms. The house has been upgraded over the years and benefits from insulated cavity walls, oil-fired central heating and double-glazed windows. A substantial detached garage, with high ceilings and a mezzanine level, provides excellent storage and offers numerous possibilities for hobbies, a workshop, home gym or other ancillary uses. The gardens are a particular feature, richly planted with mature trees and shrubs, while the rear enjoys a wonderful sunny aspect. A patio, water feature and extensive lawns create a superb setting for alfresco dining, gardening, children's play and relaxed family life.\n\nA Compelling Development Opportunity: In addition to its appeal as a family residence, White Gables House and its extensive grounds offer clear potential as a residential development site, subject to planning permission. The property occupies a strategic position between the established residential developments of Rathmichael Manor and Parc na Silla and benefits from excellent transport connections and proximity to essential services. The owners commissioned a Development Potential Assessment from Brock McClure Planning and Development Consultants, which is available upon request. The report identifies the site as zoned A1, with the objective \"to provide for new residential communities and Sustainable Neighbourhood Infrastructure in accordance with approved local area plans.\" It also notes that, given the site's existing use as one residential dwelling, a proposal for increased residential density at this location would be consistent with the National Planning Framework.\n\nLocation: The property is within walking distance of Shankill Village, with its selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. Shankill DART station and the Luas Green Line at Cherrywood provide convenient connections to Dublin city and surrounding employment centres, while the Quality Bus Corridor offers further public transport options. The M50 and N11 are readily accessible, and Loughlinstown Hospital is just moments away. Families are also well served by nearby schools, sports clubs and recreational amenities, including scenic coastal and woodland walks.\n\nProperty Highlights\n• Attractive detached family residence built in 1953\n• Located within a gated private community\n• Approximately 350 sq. m. of spacious accommodation\n• Set on approximately 1 acre of private, secluded grounds\n• Electric entrance gates and sweeping tarmac driveway\n• Generous on-site parking area\n• Spacious and well-proportioned reception rooms\n• Five bedrooms and three bathrooms\n• Upgraded over the years\n• Insulated cavity walls\n• Oil-fired central heating and double-glazed windows\n• Substantial detached garage with high ceilings and mezzanine level\n• Mature gardens with established trees and shrubs\n• Sunny rear aspect with patio, water feature and extensive lawns\n• Walking distance to Shankill Village, shops, cafés and restaurants\n• Excellent access to the DART, Luas, Quality Bus Corridor, N11 and M50\n• Management company fees. Circa 1,000 to 1,200 per annum.\n• Significant residential development potential, subject to planning permission.\n\nDevelopment disclaimer: White Gables House is offered for sale without planning permission for redevelopment. Any development proposal will be subject to obtaining all necessary planning permissions, consents and approvals. The Development Potential Assessment is available upon request and is provided for information purposes only; it does not constitute a guarantee that planning permission will be granted."
